# Values baked into every production-mode build (`npm run build`), including
# Vercel's. Committed on purpose: VITE_ values are public — they ship inside
# the JavaScript bundle — so there is nothing secret here, and having the API
# URL in version control means a build can never silently fall back to the
# localhost default and ship a site that calls the visitor's own machine.
#
# A real environment variable still wins over this file, so anything set in
# Vercel's dashboard overrides it — that is how you point Preview deployments
# at a staging API while Production uses the value below.
#
# Secrets never belong here. See .env.example.

VITE_API_URL=https://backend.famesync.com/api

# Not set here: it differs per environment and you may want the Google console
# to see a single origin. Set VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in the Vercel dashboard.
